        "id": 7350,
        "name": "savagegreywolf",
        "username": "savagegreywolf",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/3ec8ea/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-14T02:08:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>quick question: when Miss Information flips at the start of the villain turn, after that does she immediately destroy a clue card, or does she do that on the start of the next turn?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I know the 'start' of the turn does not conclude until all cards that say 'start of the villain turn' are completed but does the particular action of Miss Information destroying a clue card happen right away? it seems it would be 'better' for her if it did not do so immediately, depending on the Clues in play.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:37.102Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 7349,
        "topic_slug": "miss-information-flips",
        "display_username": "savagegreywolf",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
